# terminal-hub config: a bash file at ~/.config/terminal-hub/config.
# Places take effect at once (terminal-hub reads this every time it lists or attaches). The app
# settings are built into the page by install.sh, so run it again after changing those.

# Places whose tmux sessions are listed, in this order. The first is "here": links without a place
# (/?arg=NAME, /?arg=new) open there. KEY appears in links (/?arg=KEY:NAME); LABEL and COLOUR are
# how the place is shown.
#   place KEY LABEL COLOUR local            tmux on this machine, as you
#   place KEY LABEL COLOUR ssh HOST [CMD]   tmux on HOST over ssh (key login; HOST can be an alias
#                                           from ~/.ssh/config). CMD runs tmux there, for example
#                                           `sudo -u USER -H` for another user's sessions
#   place KEY LABEL COLOUR via CMD          tmux through CMD, a command that runs a shell command
#                                           string, for example `sudo -n -u USER bash -c` for
#                                           another user on this machine
# KEY: letters, digits, - and _. The words of CMD can't contain spaces.
place here "$(hostname)" '#7ee787' local
# place server server '#ff7b72' ssh myserver
# place bot    bot    '#d2a8ff' ssh myserver sudo -u bot -H

# Icons (optional): a place's mark in the list, in its colour. A Lucide icon name from the
# README's list (laptop, server, bot, code, ...) or an emoji. Without one, a coloured dot.
#   icon KEY NAME
# icon here laptop
# icon server server

# Categories (optional) group sessions above the places, say one per project. A session goes
# into the first category with a pattern that matches it, unless you move it from its ⋯ menu:
#   a pattern with a / matches the folder the session started in    '*/work/*'
#   one with a : matches PLACE:NAME                                  'server:deploy*'
#   any other matches the session's name                             'notes'
# Patterns are globs (* and ?). Categories with no sessions don't show.
#   category KEY LABEL ICON [PATTERN...]
# category work Work briefcase '*/work/*'
# category ops  Ops  rocket    'server:*'

# The installable app.
HUB_NAME='terminal hub'               # home-screen name and page title
HUB_SHORT_NAME='hub'                  # label under the icon
HUB_APP_ID='hub'                      # the app's identity: change it and phones see a new app
HUB_DESCRIPTION='Every tmux session in one list'

# If this machine doesn't answer within 4 s, the installed app opens this URL instead, say the
# same hub on an always-on server. Empty turns it off.
HUB_FALLBACK=''
HUB_FALLBACK_NAME=''                  # shown while switching, e.g. 'the server'
